tive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that resolve_os_actor() takes the tracker/root directory and scopes its git user.email lookup to it (matching `git -C <tracker>` today), so the shared resolver preserves each caller's git-identity resolution rather than resolving against cwd.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["bridge_repair.py:77-84 `git -C str(tracker) config user.email`","tracker_maintenance.py:129 `email = _git(tracker, 'config', 'user.email')` where `_git(tracker: str, *args)`","Plan describes `resolve_os_actor()` with no directory parameter; both callers scope git to the tracker dir, so an unscoped resolver changes which identity is returned"],"finding":"The shared resolve_os_actor() (git identity > $USER > unknown) proposed for the two USER reads omits the directory-scoping that both current call sites depend on: bridge_repair._actor runs `git -C str(tracker) config user.email` and tracker_maintenance._actor runs `_git(tracker, 'config', 'user.email')`, both scoped to the tracker directory. A resolve_os_actor() that runs git without that dir (or against cwd) would resolve a different or empty git identity, silently changing the audit actor — a behavioral delta not covered by the plan's 'behavior preserved' claim.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6383fcb9cf3bd8af","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Cut targets — '2 USER ... CUT to a shared OWNED resolve_os_actor() in config.py (git identity > $USER > unknown)'","norm_id":"n6a9ad2d722fdba0d","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A repo whose cwd git identity differs from the tracker-dir git identity (or where tracker is a separate/relocated store per EV-3b) resolves a different actor after the cut","CI where cwd has no git config but the tracker dir does (or vice versa) flips between the git email and $USER/unknown"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Define resolve_os_actor(root: str | os.PathLike[str]) -> str that runs the git user.email lookup scoped to `root` (as `git -C <root>`), and have both _actor call sites pass their existing tracker directory; state in the plan that this preserves the dir-scoped git resolution.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a proving step (grep/AST audit or a per-read note) demonstrating each of the 24 reads is resolved once at entry, OR a fixture that sets the env AFTER composition and asserts unchanged behavior, so the compose-once decision is verified rather than only asserted.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2833,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Preserve resolution timing: a read resolved LIVE per operation must be cut to a resolver that ALSO reads env live per call'","'None of these 24 is live-per-operation'","'Env-setting tests that only set REBAR_ROOT/